  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>St. George's University is an international university located in Grenada, West Indies. It is one of the worldâ€™s leading institutions for medical education, veterinary medicine, public health, and other health sciences programs.</p><p>The University attracts talented international students from over 140 countries worldwide to provide a vibrant community of determined future graduates.</p> <p> Students can also make use of the recreational amenities, such as the fitness center, sports fields and student common areas, all of which promote a healthy and active lifestyle. The True Blue campus includes a research institute set against the backdrop of the lapis blue waters of the Caribbean Sea.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Campus life at St. George's University in Grenada offers a rich and varied experience for international students. Students have the opportunity to engage in a wide range of extracurricular activities, clubs, and organisations, from the Canadian Studentâ€™s Association to the Business Studentâ€™s Association and more. The University organises events throughout the academic year, including social gatherings, guest lectures, and workshops, enhancing the overall campus experience. The campus itself was built from a $250 million investment.</p><p>The West Indies is a subregion of North America, surrounded by the North Atlantic Ocean and the Caribbean Sea. As such, the natural beauty on offer is breathtaking and highly motivating to students attempting to make a difference in the world. Grenada offers opportunities for students to explore the island, indulge in outdoor activities, and immerse themselves in the local culture.</p>"
    ],
